# The composed layers whose remainder has no figure at all. One row per composed layer whose own
# `n - d` is not its remainder and whose pivot is not owed.
#
# Two ways to have a remainder, and neither is open
#   A composed layer's remainder is its own crossed `n - d` where that difference is legitimate, or
#   the pivot `F Φ r - e_n + e_d` where it is owed. composition/unsettled.sqlc names the layers
#   where the first is not legitimate: a conversion with width scales both totals, so the
#   difference counts the factor's spread twice (`asrt:Part`: a converted remainder is "never
#   re-derived"). composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc names the layers where the second is
#   lifted. A layer in both has no figure the model can stand behind, and a fallback to `n - d`
#   would hand every remainder rule the figure `asrt:Part` refuses.
#
# A set of its own, for the depth of the plan
#   layers/remainder.sqlc drops these rows and arithmetic/remainder.sqlc says why. A filter there
#   that tested the pivot join itself re-plans every rule above it several levels deeper, past what
#   a plan read back when those statements are checked at compile time can nest; testing against
#   this set does not.
-- composition/unsettled.sqlc within composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc.
SELECT o.filing, o.layer
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc)
) o
JOIN      (
    :compose(composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc)
) l ON l.composition = o.filing AND l.composed_layer = o.layer
